<title>USA: Bradley Real Estate buys shopping centers.</title>
<headline>Bradley Real Estate buys shopping centers.</headline>
<dateline>NORTHBROOK, Ill. 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bradley Real Estate Trust Inc said Thursday it bought shopping centers in Indiana, Kansas, Iowa and Minnesota for a total of about $25 million.</p>
<p>The real estate investment trust said the properties will add about 379,000 square feet to its portfolio. Bradley added that the four centers are all at least 94-percent leased.</p>
<p>Bradley owns a total of 35 properties in 13 states.</p>
<p>Its shares were unchanged Thursday at 17-7/8.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
</text>
